            "output": "<path>C:\\Users\\g.makindu.mokonzi\\OneDrive - Accenture\\Desktop\\traccar-web\\.bench-work\\2026-10-19T19-52-35-609Z\\project\\README.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # [Traccar Web App](https://www.traccar.org)\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: \n5: This is the browser-based tracking dashboard for [Traccar](https://www.traccar.org), a free and open source GPS tracking platform. It's a React, Material UI, and MapLibre single-page app that talks to the [Traccar server](https://github.com/traccar/traccar) over its REST API, providing the live map, reports, geofences, and device management UI most people mean when they say \"Traccar.\"\n6: \n7: This repository is the front-end only. For the back-end server, see the [main Traccar repository](https://github.com/traccar/traccar). You don't need to build this yourself to use Traccar - the server repository already bundles a built copy - this repo is for contributing to or customizing the UI itself.\n8: \n9: [Try the live demo](https://www.traccar.org/demo-server/) without installing anything.\n10: \n11: | Web Dashboard |\n12: |---|\n13: | ![Traccar web dashboard](.github/screenshot.png) |\n14: \n15: ## Development\n16: \n17: ```shell\n18: npm install\n19: npm start\n20: ```\n21: \n22: This starts a local dev server (Vite) that proxies API requests to a running Traccar server. See the [web app build documentation](https://www.traccar.org/build-web-app/) for full setup details, including how to point it at your own server.\n23: \n24: To build a production bundle:\n25: \n26: ```shell\n27: npm run build\n28: ```\n29: \n30: ## OpenCode benchmark\n31: \n32: The current branch, `benchmark/opencode-on-no-routing`, runs OpenCode with the `context-mode` plugin enabled and without explicit Context Mode routing instructions. Its [`opencode.json`](opencode.json) loads only the shared [`.opencode/instructions.md`](.opencode/instructions.md). The routing configuration and `.opencode/context-mode-routing.md` file have been removed from this branch.\n33: \n34: This branch is compared with `benchmark/opencode-on-plus-routing`, which enables the same plugin with explicit routing instructions, and `benchmark/opencode-off`, which disables the plugin. The campaign runner lives on `benchmark/opencode-runner`.\n35: \n36: ## Benchmark team\n37: \n38: - Makindu Kenzi — [GitHub](https://github.com/KnMvstr) · [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/in/makindu-kenzi/)\n39: \n40: ## License\n41: \n42: Apache License, Version 2.0. See [LICENSE.txt](https://github.com/traccar/traccar-web/blob/master/LICENSE.txt) for details.\n\n(End of file - total 42 lines)\n</content>",
